      "text": "To determine the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we need to first calculate the total number of rounds played by all the golfers and then divide by the total number of golfers.\n\nFrom the chart, we can see the number of rounds played by each golfer is as follows:\n- 1: 5 golfers\n- 2: 2 golfers\n- 3: 2 golfers\n- 4: 3 golfers\n- 5: 5 golfers\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of rounds played:\n\\[\n5 \\times 1 + 2 \\times 2 + 2 \\times 3 + 3 \\times 4 + 5 \\times 5 = 5 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25 = 52\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total number of golfers:\n\\[\n5 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5 = 17\n\\]\n\nThe average number of rounds played by each golfer is the total number of rounds divided by the total number of golfers:\n\\[\n\\frac{52}{17} \\approx 3.05882352941\n\\]\n\nRounding 3.05882352941 to the nearest whole number, we get:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
