      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golf player, we need to calculate the total number of rounds played and then divide by the total number of golfers. From the chart, we can see that:\n\n- 5 golfers played 1 round each.\n- 2 golfers played 2 rounds each.\n- 2 golfers played 3 rounds each.\n- 3 golfers played 4 rounds each.\n- 5 golfers played 5 rounds each.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of rounds played:\n\\[\n5 \\times 1 + 2 \\times 2 + 2 \\times 3 + 3 \\times 4 + 5 \\times 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= 5 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25\n\\]\n\\[\n= 52\n\\]\nNext, we calculate the total number of golfers:\n\\[\n5 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5 = 17\n\\]\nThe average number of rounds played by each golfer is the total number of rounds divided by the total number of golfers:\n\\[\n\\frac{52}{17} \\approx 3.0882\n\\]\nRounding 3.0882 to the nearest whole number, we get:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
