    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we need to:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of rounds played.\n2. Calculate the total number of golfers.\n3. Divide the total number of rounds by the total number of golfers to find the average.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of rounds played.**\n\nFrom the chart, we can see the number of rounds played for each number of golfers:\n- 1 golfer played 5 rounds.\n- 2 golfers played 2 rounds each.\n- 3 golfers played 2 rounds each.\n- 4 golfers played 3 rounds each.\n- 5 golfers played 5 rounds each.\n\nNow, we sum these values:\n\\[ 5 \\text{ (rounds by 1 golfer)} + 2 \\times 2 \\text{ (rounds by 2 golfers)} + 3 \\times 2 \\text{ (rounds by 3 golfers)} + 4 \\times 3 \\text{ (rounds by 4 golfers)} + 5 \\times 5 \\text{ (rounds by 5 golfers)} \\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\\[ 5 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25 = 54 \\]\n\nSo, the total number of rounds played is 54.\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the total number of golfers.**\n\nFrom the chart, we can see the number of golfers for each number of rounds played:\n- 1 golfer played 5 rounds.\n- 2 golfers played 2 rounds each.\n- 3 golfers played 2 rounds each.\n- 4 golfers played 3 rounds each.\n- 5 golfers played 5 rounds each.\n\nFrom this:\n- 1 golfer = 1 golfer\n- 2 golfers = 2 golfers\n- 3 golfers = 3 golfers\n- 4 golfers = 4 golfers\n- 5 golfers = 5 golfers\n\nAdding these together, we get:\n\\[ 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 = 15 \\]\n\nSo, the total number of golfers is 15.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the average number of rounds played.**\n\nThe average is found by dividing the total number of rounds by the total number of golfers:\n\\[ \\text{Average} = \\frac{\\text{Total number of rounds}}{\\text{Total number of golfers}} = \\frac{54}{15} \\]\n\nSimplifying the fraction:\n\\[ \\frac{54}{15} \\approx 3.6 \\]\n\nRounding 3.6 to the nearest whole number, we get:\n\\[ 4 \\]\n\nThus, the average number of rounds played by each golfer is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).",
