      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we need to divide the total number of rounds played by the total number of golfers. \n\nFrom the chart, we can see that there are 5 golfers who played 1 round, 2 golfers who played 2 rounds, 2 golfers who played 3 rounds, 3 golfers who played 4 rounds, and 5 golfers who played 5 rounds. \n\nTo calculate the total number of rounds played, we can use the formula:\n\nTotal rounds = (Number of golfers in each group * Number of rounds played by each group)\n\nTotal rounds = (5 * 1) + (2 * 2) + (2 * 3) + (3 * 4) + (5 * 5)\n                 = 5 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25\n                 = 52\n\nTo find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we can use the formula:\n\nAverage = Total rounds / Total number of golfers\n\nAverage = 52 / 15\n        ≈ 3.47\n\nTo express the average to the nearest whole number, we round 3.47 to 3.\n\nTherefore, the average number of rounds played by each golfer is \\boxed{3}.",
